<article class="env-lemma" id="09E5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09E5">Lemma <span data-tag="09E5">15.113.2</span>.</a> Let $A \subset B$ be an extension of discrete valuation rings with fraction fields $K \subset L$. If the extension $L/K$ is finite, then the residue field extension is finite and we have $ef \leq [L : K]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Finiteness of the residue field extension is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/031F" data-tag="031F">10.119.10</a>. The inequality follows from Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/00PE" data-tag="00PE">10.119.9</a> and <a href="/tag/02M0" data-tag="02M0">10.52.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>